  "title": "Articles",
  "emoji": "📝",
  "parentNote": "Articles (a, an, the) are small but very important! The trick: \"a\" before consonant sounds, \"an\" before vowel sounds (a, e, i, o, u). Practice with objects around the house: \"a cup, an apple, the sun.\"",
  "learnBullets": [
    "What **articles** are — small words (a, an, the) used before nouns",
    "When to use **\"a\"** (before consonant sounds)",
    "When to use **\"an\"** (before vowel sounds)",
    "When to use **\"the\"** (for specific things)"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**What are Articles?**\nArticles are small words that come before nouns. There are only THREE articles in English:\n- **a** (for general things, consonant sounds)\n- **an** (for general things, vowel sounds)\n- **the** (for specific things)\n\n**A vs An — The Sound Rule:**\n\n| Use | When the next word starts with | Examples |\n|-----|-------------------------------|----------|\n| **a** | consonant sound (b, c, d, f, g, h, j, k, l, m, n, p, q, r, s, t, v, w, x, y, z) | a ball, a cat, a dog |\n| **an** | vowel sound (a, e, i, o, u) | an apple, an egg, an ice cream |\n\n**Special Cases:**\n- **an** hour (h is silent, sounds like \"our\")\n- **a** university (u sounds like \"you\" — consonant sound)\n- **an** umbrella (u sounds like \"uh\" — vowel sound)\n\n**When to use \"the\":**\n- When there is **only one** of something: the sun, the moon\n- When we are talking about **something specific**: the book on the table\n- When we **already mentioned** it: I saw a cat. **The** cat was white.\n\n### 🧠 How to Choose the Right Article\n1. **Listen** to the SOUND of the next word (not just the letter)\n2. **Vowel sound** → an\n3. **Consonant sound** → a\n4. **Specific/Only one** → the\n\n---",
